    <item>
      <title>Descend</title>
      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/734679</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/734679#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">4d8f9350208693e059746452e1735a5404d9efe8</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:04:58 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0b264c6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bc3775.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0ba1986.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0b80f7c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bb9b53.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bd88f5.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0bce35c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae63b0ae9503.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Descend&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;Activate Ascend normally, click L3 and you can now descend to ceilings beneath you rather than merely ascend through ceilings above you. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The descend marker will (try to) help you by changing from red to green based on how close you are to "descend-able" ground. It doesn't work terribly well. The game just isn't designed around the concept of descending unlike ascend. But I still find it's better than having only an on/off detector. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The mod is an exefs-patch/ipchtxt, so it doesn't occupy a subsdk slot and can be used with other mods mostly conflict-free (unless they are dealing with similar concepts like another ascend mod). &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Installation&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Emulator: extract the &lt;b&gt;descend&lt;/b&gt; folder into the game's mod directory and enable Descend.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Atmosphere: copy the archive's &lt;b&gt;exefs_patches/descend&lt;/b&gt; folder into &lt;b&gt;atmosphere/exefs_patches/descend&lt;/b&gt; on the SD card.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Link's feet sometimes don't appear at the descend destination, particularly when the exit is sloped or jagged.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The camera can sometimes appear inside of a wall, revealing an "out of bounds" area when previewing an exit at your destination. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In rare instances, you may wind up inside of a wall/out-of-bounds area. Warping to a shrine is your only option here.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Animations/Swirling can look janky at times. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Limitations&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;b&gt;Only tested on Switch running v1.2.1 of the game. Highly unlikely to work on other versions.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;AI Disclaimer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This project was developed with heavy help from AI Codex Astra 6. For an overview of how I develop ExeFS mods using AI please see this post &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739"&gt;https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Donations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you enjoy my work, feel free to &lt;a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/hansoloblaster" target="_blank"&gt;buy me a coffee&lt;/a&gt;! I provide the mod and its source code completely free and open source. I stand by that; so only donate if you're feeling friendly or would like to boost my spirits!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/descend-v0150.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>Gameplay</category>
      <category>Gameplay</category>
    </item>
