      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae49fde2a32d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae4a018e8c50.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; TCR is back in Totk!&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;TCR now supports passive markers. When Link is attacked, the TCR is actively triggered, and Link will pursue the last target that attacked him.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: Add a passive marker&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;This allows you to perform TCR just like in BotW. The trick requires the same setup: pull your bow at a sufficient height, &lt;b&gt;hold down ZR the entire time, quickly press B to cancel, then press Y. Once you land, it will actively trigger a Flurry Rush attacking the target locked by ZL. &lt;/b&gt;Unlike in BotW, there is no need to mark the enemy beforehand, and the button inputs are slightly different. But either way, TCR has now been successfully implemented in TotK!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Note: This only supports version 1.2.1 and has only been tested on emulators.&lt;/b&gt;</description>
